---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
const updated = '2026-11-11';
---

<Base title="Terms of use" description="Terms for using PQC Deps, its data and its API.">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <h2>What this is</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE.name} is a free, community-maintained catalog of public information about post-quantum
      cryptography support in open-source software. It's provided for information only.
    </p>

    <h2>Not security advice</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Entries summarize public sources and can be incomplete, out of date or wrong. Always check
        the linked sources and the library's own documentation before relying on them.
      </li>
      <li>
        A library supporting an algorithm doesn't mean your software uses it. You may still need to
        upgrade, configure or call new APIs.
      </li>
      <li>
        The dependency checker matches names and versions only. It doesn't analyze your code.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The site, data and tools are provided <strong>"as is", without warranty of any kind</strong>,
      and the maintainers aren't liable for decisions made using them.
    </p>

    <h2>Using the data and code</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Catalog data (including <code>/api/catalog.json</code>) is licensed
        <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a>: reuse it freely,
        crediting {SITE.name} with a link.
      </li>
      <li>The source code is licensed MIT.</li>
      <li>
        Library names and trademarks belong to their owners. Listing a library doesn't imply any
        affiliation or endorsement.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Fair use of the site</h2>
    <p>
      Don't abuse the request forms (spam, automated submissions, offensive content) or try to
      disrupt the service. We may remove requests and block abuse. Please cache the JSON API
      rather than polling it heavily.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      Spotted a mistake? Use <em>Suggest a correction</em> on any library page or open an issue on
      <a href={SITE.repoUrl}>GitHub</a>. Maintainers of listed libraries are especially welcome.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>These terms may change; the date above shows the latest version.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
